SRC/shar -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  shar.c   getpat() tested each file with               if (access(ptr,S_IOREAD) || access(ptr,S_IREAD)) {} else error           which is backwards -- access() answers 0 when it CAN -- and the           port's own comment said so ("The logic here is mucked up.           Change it later.--Jim O.").  So shar answered `No read access           for file' for every file it could read and wrapped only files           it could not.  It is now  if (access(ptr,S_IREAD)) error.           `extern char *ctime()' is fenced with #ifndef ctime, because           this SDK's <time.h> makes ctime() a macro.  Rebuilt -qm,           2026-09-26.  The original is shar.c.ori.           The port's `#define fputc putc' is removed, so the line end           after each file's `SHAR_EOF' is written by the library's own           fputc.  Through the putc macro that one byte never reached           the output, the delimiter ran into `#  End of shell archive',           and sh would have read past the end of the file.  Measured           with dump on the archive before and after, 2026-09-26.